  "problems": [
    "G3: the loud layer is not brighter than the soft one (v1 0.324, v2 0.125); expected for soft bowing, whose first 300 ms is mostly bow noise before the tone builds, so the measure reads it as bright",
    "B3: the loud layer is not brighter than the soft one (v1 0.296, v2 0.114); expected for soft bowing, whose first 300 ms is mostly bow noise before the tone builds, so the measure reads it as bright",
    "D4: the loud layer is not brighter than the soft one (v1 0.321, v2 0.061); expected for soft bowing, whose first 300 ms is mostly bow noise before the tone builds, so the measure reads it as bright",
    "C5: the loud layer is not brighter than the soft one (v1 0.268, v2 0.230); expected for soft bowing, whose first 300 ms is mostly bow noise before the tone builds, so the measure reads it as bright",
    "E5: the loud layer is not brighter than the soft one (v1 0.559, v2 0.505); expected for soft bowing, whose first 300 ms is mostly bow noise before the tone builds, so the measure reads it as bright",
    "sus/G5-v2 (VlnEns_susVib_G4_v2.wav): pitch: frame tracker -0.3 c and spectrum comb +9.2 c disagree (the comb reads the vibrato-smeared average spectrum; the frame tracker's median is used)",
    "G5: the loud layer is not brighter than the soft one (v1 0.756, v2 0.383); expected for soft bowing, whose first 300 ms is mostly bow noise before the tone builds, so the measure reads it as bright",
    "zones further apart than a whole tone, by design (the kit brief thins to about a minor third; a note is played from the nearer zone, at most 2 semitones away): G3 to B3 (4), B3 to D4 (3), D4 to Fs4 (4), Fs4 to A4 (3), A4 to C5 (3), C5 to E5 (4), E5 to G5 (3), G5 to B5 (4), B5 to D6 (3)",
    "soft swells: in 6 files the source takes over 3 s to settle, so the loop starts late and the file is longer: sus/B3-v1 (loop from 3.71 s), sus/D4-v1 (loop from 3.44 s), sus/C5-v1 (loop from 3.55 s), sus/E5-v1 (loop from 3.09 s), sus/G5-v1 (loop from 4.22 s), sus/B5-v1 (loop from 4.08 s)",
    "m4a files decode 52 to 961 samples (1 to 20 ms) longer than the .ogg because AAC pads its last frame; their start is not shifted (lag 0 against the processed file), so the same loop times hold and loop.endS, not the file end, must be the loop end"
  ]
}
